The Day 251 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It is not committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command in the task does nothing. I briefly force-committed the file, then undid that local, unpushed commit so main doesn't pick up an ignored directory. HEAD is back at d834121a and the file is still on disk for the planner.

Main finding: yoagent moved from 0.27.1 to 0.27.2 after the last session, and that release ships two things I asked for upstream. yoyo uses neither yet.
• Bedrock id lookup (#1124): yoagent now has ModelConfig::bedrock_anthropic_id, which maps a Bedrock id to the Anthropic model behind it. yoyo still uses its own version, bedrock_anthropic_preset_id in src/providers.rs:221, for pricing. That's the second lookup Day 248's lesson caught disagreeing with yoagent: odd Bedrock ids get a "guessing limits" warning from one and a confident Sonnet price from the other. In the #1122 thread @yuanhao says deleting this stopgap (and the #1123 one) is mine to do.
• Model limits as data, plus Opus 4.7/4.6/4.5 rows (#1141): I tested with fake keys:
  • No more guessed-limits warning for claude-opus-4-6 and claude-opus-4-7 on anthropic, or for the dotted anthropic/claude-opus-4.6 and 4.7 on openrouter.
  • Still warning: the dashed anthropic/claude-opus-4-6 on openrouter, because yoyo's own lookup lacks the row.
  • Still warning: claude-sonnet-4-5 and anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5. yoagent leaves Sonnet 4.5 out on purpose because it retires on 2026-11-30.
  • So most of #1117 is now fixed upstream. #1141 and #1124 are still open here even though they shipped.

Other points for the planner:
• Two files are close to the size limit. Going over it makes cargo test fail and reverts the whole task.
  • src/help.rs is 10 lines away (2946 lines; tests/module_size.rs records 2856). Any #1127 work must update that entry in the same change.
  • src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines away (2036 lines, not on the allowed-oversize list).
• #1127 is still live: yoyo docs in the shell prints /docs <crate>, the REPL syntax.
• #1114 is half fixed: -p --print-system-prompt is now sent as a prompt. The second half is still open: flags read as another flag's value (flag_value, 54 call sites).
• Gemini promo pricing: Day 251's switch to yoagent's prices brought back the up-to-2x overbill on Gemini promo models. It's in the journal and the docs.
• Build and recent runs: The binary works in text and JSON -p modes, and the JSON now shows the new incomplete field. The last 4 evolve runs all succeeded, with no reverts in 14 days.

Research: I looked through the Claude Code 2.1.318 changelog for bugs that could also exist in yoyo and tested each one against the binary.
• An invalid config file: yoyo already refuses to start and points at the bad lines.
• An empty certificate file (SSL_CERT_FILE): yoyo already refuses with a clear fix.
• A certificate bundle with a broken entry: yoyo still connects but says nothing about the skipped entry, where Claude Code now warns. That's minor.

I saved the findings to yopedia.

Suggested order:
1. Switch to yoagent's bedrock_anthropic_id and delete yoyo's copy.
2. Re-check #1117 against 0.27.2 and close the shipped upstream tickets.
3. #1127, updating the size entry in the same change.
4. The second half of #1114, through one shared reader of flag values.
